event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":3013,"item_id":"fc_0aa1a57c94fa882d016ae210e4b5748191b28d55ae73f6db0b","output_index":3,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":6,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/logic/rules/-\",\"value\":\"natural_induction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/rules/-\",\"value\":\"natural_induction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/argument/@S004/text\",\"old\":\"Since 2^m≥m+1, their remainders tend to zero by the Archimedean property,\",\"new\":\"For m=0, 2^m≥m+1; the induction step follows from 2·(m+1)≥m+2 for m≥0. Thus 2^m≥m+1 for all natural m, so the remainders tend to zero by the Archimedean property,\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/argument/@S004/text\",\"old\":\"follow by finite algebra (or induction).\",\"new\":\"follow by telescoping the finite geometric sums.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family K→ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R003/modified-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For i∈K define r_i=diam(U_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"U\",\"diam\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/locals/@U/declaration\",\"value\":\"For i∈K leave W_i fixed if its diameter is positive. If it is a singleton, let U_i be the closed ball centered at its unique point, of diameter min(r/2,(ε2^{-i-3})^{1/q}); n≥1 ensures that ball has exactly this positive diameter.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/argument/@S002/text\",\"value\":\"Choose W from F001. Discard empty members and let K={i:W_i≠∅}. A nonempty zero-diameter W_i is a singleton, since distance zero identifies any two of its points. For each such i take the positive number min(r/2,(ε2^{-i-3})^{1/q}) and replace W_i by the closed ball centered at its unique point, with radius half that number. It has positive diameter at most r and q-cost ≤ε2^{-i-3}<ε2^{-i-2}; the power identity is valid because q>0. The diameter is exactly the prescribed number because n≥1: two opposite points in the first-coordinate direction belong to the closed ball, and the triangle inequality supplies the reverse diameter bound. Leave every positive-diameter member unchanged. Define U_i to be this resulting family on K and r_i=diam(U_i). The cover still contains every W_i and hence covers E, with 0<r_i≤r. Its total q-cost is at most the original cost plus Σ_{i≥0}ε2^{-i-2}≤ original cost+ε/2<ε, using the geometric sum in N001 and finite-partial-sum comparisons. This is the supplied replacement argument with an explicit permissible choice of the small diameters. Discharge L1 and universally quantify q,r,ε.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/argument/@S002/objects/-\",\"value\":\"r_i\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family K→ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R004/positive-ambient\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For i∈K put r_i=diam(U_i); N003 gives 0<r_i≤r.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N003\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"U\",\"diam\",\"r\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@K/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@U/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@N/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/objects/-\",\"value\":\"r_i\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/text\",\"old\":\"Fix q>D and δ,ε>0 (L3).\",\"new\":\"Fix q>D and δ>0 (L3), and independently fix ε>0 (L4).\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/introduces/-\",\"value\":\"L4\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/produces/0/assumptions/-\",\"value\":\"L4\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S003/text\",\"old\":\"For the fixed q and δ, the construction and F002 work for every ε>0, so\",\"new\":\"Discharge L4 and universally quantify ε in F002. For the fixed q and δ the content is bounded by 2(√2)^{q+1}ε for every ε>0, so\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S003/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L4\",\"L3\",\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@ε/declaration\",\"value\":\"Fix ε>0 under L4, independently of q and δ, and later universally quantify it.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R007/argument/@S002/text\",\"old\":\"Their supremum is D, by real order density (for example s=D(1-1/m) for integers m≥2).\",\"new\":\"Their supremum is D, by real order density.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/text\",\"old\":\"The squared distance between two concatenated tuples is\",\"new\":\"For arbitrary x,y∈V(n) and real t,u, the squared distance between the two concatenated tuples is\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"element of V(n)\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary x∈V(n) for the squared-distance identity.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"element of V(n)\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary y∈V(n) for the squared-distance identity.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any real t.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any real u.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"x\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"y\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"t\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"u\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/2\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Define f_i=ind(J_i∩I,ρ_i^s) on ℝ. Each is measurable: on the Borel set J_i∩I it is a constant and on its Borel complement it is zero; inverse images of Borel sets are therefore one of these sets, ∅, or ℝ. In particular it is λ-almost-everywhere measurable. F002 gives ind(I,c)≤Σ_i f_i pointwise on all ℝ, since outside I both sides vanish.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"I\",\"J\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"λ\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"Every f_i=ind(J_i∩I,ρ_i^s) is measurable and hence λ-almost-everywhere measurable; on all ℝ, ind(I,c)≤Σ_i f_i pointwise.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"J\",\"I\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"λ\",\"c\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/3\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"M008 applied to the pointwise inequality F003 gives the corresponding inequality of nonnegative integrals. M007 on I with c and N005's λ(I)=1 identifies the left integral with c. M006 exchanges the nonnegative sum and integral, using the measurability already proved in F003; M007 on each J_i∩I with coefficient ρ_i^s then gives c≤Σ_i ρ_i^s λ(J_i∩I). By F002 this is at most Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+Σ_i η_iρ_i^s≤Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+ε, since η_iρ_i^s=ε2^{-i-1}ρ_i^s/(1+ρ_i^s)≤ε2^{-i-1} and N001 gives Σ_i2^{-i-1}=1. The product and sum comparisons follow first for finite partial sums and then by their suprema; thus they remain valid if a series is infinite. This is Tonelli for nonnegative terms, without finite-integrability premises or an exchange of signed series.\",\"uses\":[\"M006\",\"M007\",\"M008\",\"N005\",\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"I\",\"J\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"η\",\"ε\",\"λ\",\"LInt\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"For the arbitrary ε>0 and cover W, c≤Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+ε.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"ε\",\"W\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Discharge L3 and quantify ε in F004: for every ε>0, c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε. If the series is infinite, c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1} is immediate. Otherwise it is a finite real, and order density applied to the inequality for every ε>0 gives c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}. Since W was an arbitrary δ-cover, c is a lower bound of every admissible (s+1)-cost; therefore c≤H^{s+1}_δ(F), their infimum. Discharge L2, then L1, and universally quantify s,δ. This proves the asserted inequality with exactly the same scale on both sides.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"W\",\"H\",\"F\",\"E\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\",\"L1\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@s/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@δ/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@c/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@W/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@ρ/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@ε/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/0/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/0/hypothesis_checks/1\",\"value\":\"F003 is exactly the required global pointwise inequality; its derivation from F002 included the vanishing outside I.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/1/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/1/hypothesis_checks/2\",\"value\":\"F003 proves every f_i measurable by the inverse-image argument on the Borel pieces J_i∩I and its complement; hence every f_i is λ-almost-everywhere measurable.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/2/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/3/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"}]}}"}

event: response.output_item.done
