9pkMFSuxUKrn_AroEPUD8fhu4vCa2KfipNs7vdIJuYC-EiBB-w9LQaw2JUtTaDNLkCfRrVHEg9M-FG_XgY4Io3WxY_bQnx0RyyO67J9rkgnm20lJtOOZ_n9_M86boryay2eLO5OVPlSQI4EB2W-HjRTfuneMhX3fTG7q5YcvNNsPcbta6Bmu3-7TAmmWkGK7s5BRWjuN4KIWfe_J48Zz7RbXkJw_X54mmj3H7RTq0D3W185mgn4TvxvHs8LdgM3baPACsKQd-_qE126sVU_qnW844SYJxRpfbMHGEwSVpmd9Wm2P8vMKNWaf5_jF_pkHcWBkCrzBJMra5thMhBzm7bMd0tPX0geeLafDEjNlXmTnN3VDxdiT-cdlaQ=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0aa1a57c94fa882d016ae210e4b5748191b28d55ae73f6db0b","call_id":"call_eedab07248b5463caf32513bba6c48f6","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":6,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/logic/rules/-\",\"value\":\"natural_induction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/rules/-\",\"value\":\"natural_induction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/argument/@S004/text\",\"old\":\"Since 2^m≥m+1, their remainders tend to zero by the Archimedean property,\",\"new\":\"For m=0, 2^m≥m+1; the induction step follows from 2·(m+1)≥m+2 for m≥0. Thus 2^m≥m+1 for all natural m, so the remainders tend to zero by the Archimedean property,\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R001/argument/@S004/text\",\"old\":\"follow by finite algebra (or induction).\",\"new\":\"follow by telescoping the finite geometric sums.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family K→ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R003/modified-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For i∈K define r_i=diam(U_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"U\",\"diam\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/locals/@U/declaration\",\"value\":\"For i∈K leave W_i fixed if its diameter is positive. If it is a singleton, let U_i be the closed ball centered at its unique point, of diameter min(r/2,(ε2^{-i-3})^{1/q}); n≥1 ensures that ball has exactly this positive diameter.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/argument/@S002/text\",\"value\":\"Choose W from F001. Discard empty members and let K={i:W_i≠∅}. A nonempty zero-diameter W_i is a singleton, since distance zero identifies any two of its points. For each such i take the positive number min(r/2,(ε2^{-i-3})^{1/q}) and replace W_i by the closed ball centered at its unique point, with radius half that number. It has positive diameter at most r and q-cost ≤ε2^{-i-3}<ε2^{-i-2}; the power identity is valid because q>0. The diameter is exactly the prescribed number because n≥1: two opposite points in the first-coordinate direction belong to the closed ball, and the triangle inequality supplies the reverse diameter bound. Leave every positive-diameter member unchanged. Define U_i to be this resulting family on K and r_i=diam(U_i). The cover still contains every W_i and hence covers E, with 0<r_i≤r. Its total q-cost is at most the original cost plus Σ_{i≥0}ε2^{-i-2}≤ original cost+ε/2<ε, using the geometric sum in N001 and finite-partial-sum comparisons. This is the supplied replacement argument with an explicit permissible choice of the small diameters. Discharge L1 and universally quantify q,r,ε.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R003/argument/@S002/objects/-\",\"value\":\"r_i\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family K→ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R004/positive-ambient\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For i∈K put r_i=diam(U_i); N003 gives 0<r_i≤r.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N003\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"U\",\"diam\",\"r\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@K/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@U/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@N/end\",\"value\":\"S002\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/objects/-\",\"value\":\"r_i\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/text\",\"old\":\"Fix q>D and δ,ε>0 (L3).\",\"new\":\"Fix q>D and δ>0 (L3), and independently fix ε>0 (L4).\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/introduces/-\",\"value\":\"L4\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/produces/0/assumptions/-\",\"value\":\"L4\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S003/text\",\"old\":\"For the fixed q and δ, the construction and F002 work for every ε>0, so\",\"new\":\"Discharge L4 and universally quantify ε in F002. For the fixed q and δ the content is bounded by 2(√2)^{q+1}ε for every ε>0, so\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S003/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L4\",\"L3\",\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R004/locals/@ε/declaration\",\"value\":\"Fix ε>0 under L4, independently of q and δ, and later universally quantify it.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R007/argument/@S002/text\",\"old\":\"Their supremum is D, by real order density (for example s=D(1-1/m) for integers m≥2).\",\"new\":\"Their supremum is D, by real order density.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/text\",\"old\":\"The squared distance between two concatenated tuples is\",\"new\":\"For arbitrary x,y∈V(n) and real t,u, the squared distance between the two concatenated tuples is\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"element of V(n)\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary x∈V(n) for the squared-distance identity.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"element of V(n)\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary y∈V(n) for the squared-distance identity.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any real t.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/concatenation\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any real u.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"x\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"y\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"t\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S003/objects/-\",\"value\":\"u\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/2\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Define f_i=ind(J_i∩I,ρ_i^s) on ℝ. Each is measurable: on the Borel set J_i∩I it is a constant and on its Borel complement it is zero; inverse images of Borel sets are therefore one of these sets, ∅, or ℝ. In particular it is λ-almost-everywhere measurable. F002 gives ind(I,c)≤Σ_i f_i pointwise on all ℝ, since outside I both sides vanish.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"I\",\"J\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"λ\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"Every f_i=ind(J_i∩I,ρ_i^s) is measurable and hence λ-almost-everywhere measurable; on all ℝ, ind(I,c)≤Σ_i f_i pointwise.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"J\",\"I\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"λ\",\"c\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/3\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"M008 applied to the pointwise inequality F003 gives the corresponding inequality of nonnegative integrals. M007 on I with c and N005's λ(I)=1 identifies the left integral with c. M006 exchanges the nonnegative sum and integral, using the measurability already proved in F003; M007 on each J_i∩I with coefficient ρ_i^s then gives c≤Σ_i ρ_i^s λ(J_i∩I). By F002 this is at most Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+Σ_i η_iρ_i^s≤Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+ε, since η_iρ_i^s=ε2^{-i-1}ρ_i^s/(1+ρ_i^s)≤ε2^{-i-1} and N001 gives Σ_i2^{-i-1}=1. The product and sum comparisons follow first for finite partial sums and then by their suprema; thus they remain valid if a series is infinite. This is Tonelli for nonnegative terms, without finite-integrability premises or an exchange of signed series.\",\"uses\":[\"M006\",\"M007\",\"M008\",\"N005\",\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"ind\",\"I\",\"J\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"η\",\"ε\",\"λ\",\"LInt\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"For the arbitrary ε>0 and cover W, c≤Σ_i ρ_i^{s+1}+ε.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"ε\",\"W\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Discharge L3 and quantify ε in F004: for every ε>0, c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε. If the series is infinite, c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1} is immediate. Otherwise it is a finite real, and order density applied to the inequality for every ε>0 gives c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}. Since W was an arbitrary δ-cover, c is a lower bound of every admissible (s+1)-cost; therefore c≤H^{s+1}_δ(F), their infimum. Discharge L2, then L1, and universally quantify s,δ. This proves the asserted inequality with exactly the same scale on both sides.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"W\",\"H\",\"F\",\"E\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\",\"L1\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@s/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@δ/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@c/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@W/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@ρ/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/locals/@ε/end\",\"value\":\"S005\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/0/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/0/hypothesis_checks/1\",\"value\":\"F003 is exactly the required global pointwise inequality; its derivation from F002 included the vanishing outside I.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/1/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/1/hypothesis_checks/2\",\"value\":\"F003 proves every f_i measurable by the inverse-image argument on the Borel pieces J_i∩I and its complement; hence every f_i is λ-almost-everywhere measurable.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/2/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/@R006/applications/3/at\",\"value\":\"S004\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_ch